From 09a87026638efef858d4ba2fc2a9263ea409183f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Antoine Martin <dev@ayakael.net>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 18:03:33 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 022/107] u-boot-clockworkpi-uconsole-radxa-cm5: set serial
 output to uart4

By default, u-boot sends serial output to uart2. This sometimes causes
boot issues due to some uConsole modules using uart2 to function. In
addition, it is possible to access serial output via GPIO FPC connector.

This commit changes serial output to that GPIO connector, allowing
better access to serial output and removing conflict with certain
modules (notably HackerGadget's)

Vendor u-boot usually takes its uart settings from SPL or BL31, which
defaults to uart2. To use the uart settings from defconfig, we disable
preloader settings by unsetting CONFIG_ROCKCHIP_PRELOADER_SERIAL

Part-of: <https://gitlab.nura.eco/nura/pmaports/-/merge_requests/8285>
---
 .../0004-rk3588-serial-output-s4.patch        | 39 +++++++++++++++++++
 .../APKBUILD                                  |  4 +-
